st":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":56.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.35501018484657854,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05358924286918754,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":51.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04978887164144881,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":66.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.021679741209709835,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":77.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013289598352726431,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.01578,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"S&T Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for S&T Bank that provides retail and commercial banking products and services to consumer, commercial, and small businesses in Pennsylvania and Ohio. It accepts time and demand deposits; originates commercial and consumer loans; and cash management, brokerage, and trust services, as well as act as guardian of employee benefits. The company also manages private investment accounts for individuals and institutions. In addition, it engages in non-banking activities; and acts as a reinsurer of credit life, accident, and health insurance policies. S&T Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1902 and is headquartered in Indiana, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher J. McComish | CEO & Chairman | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $333K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $107K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["S&T Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.8B market cap on $402M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $129M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 1.00\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 37% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"S&T Bancorp (NASDAQ:STBA) Sets New 12-Month High \u2013 Should You Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/st-bancorp-nasdaqstba-sets-new-12-month-high-should-you-buy.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894513.0,"origin":"tiingo","sent